# Cursor Rules for PDN Chat Project

## Git and Version Control
- NEVER commit code automatically without explicit user approval
- ALWAYS show changes first using `git diff` or `git show` before committing
- ALWAYS ask "Should I proceed with these changes?" before any commit
- Use `git add` and `git commit` as separate steps, never combined
- Wait for user confirmation before pushing to remote repository

## Code Changes
- Show exactly what files will be modified before making changes
- Explain the purpose and impact of each change
- Use descriptive commit messages when user approves commits
- Prefer small, focused commits over large changes

## Communication
- Always explain what I'm about to do before doing it
- Ask for permission before making any destructive changes
- Provide clear summaries of all changes made
- Be explicit about the scope and impact of modifications

## Safety
- Never force push without explicit permission
- Always backup important changes before major modifications
- Respect the user's workflow and preferences
- Prioritize code safety and stability over speed
